  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A prefixed name in an element()/attribute() kind test (e.g. self::attribute(x:expand-text), where x is declared on an ancestor xsl:* element) now resolves its prefix against the stylesheet's namespaces and matches the intended nodes, instead of raising a spurious XPST0081 at parse time (reported by Martin Honnen, running XSpec). Streaming (XSLT 3.0 §19 posture/sweep): a large batch of streamable xsl:copy / xsl:copy-of / copy-of() / snapshot() shapes now stream correctly — a for-each of streamed attributes captured into a typed attribute()* variable; mixed streamed+grounded for-each selects; copy-namespaces=\"yes\" preserving ancestor in-scope namespaces on a copied streamed element; a leading copy-of(path)/snapshot(path) for-each select; a nested/navigating xsl:copy select that must buffer; and apply-templates select=\"copy-of()\" switching modes on the matched subtree (Saxon bug 2630). Document nodes constructed into element content transmit their content (concatenated) rather than being atomized/space-separated, while the same nodes captured into a variable and atomized keep separation. Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.3.0 and PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 1.6.1. No breaking API changes. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
